# ASR-02: Research Existing ASR Models and Architectures

**Project:** Kashmiri Voice AI  
**Task ID:** ASR-02  
**Assigned To:** Person A  
**Priority:** High  
**Status:** Initial Research and Model Collection

## 1. Objective

The objective of ASR-02 is to identify and collect existing pretrained Automatic Speech Recognition models that can recognize Kashmiri speech and produce text in Perso-Arabic script.

Instead of immediately developing a new model, the project will investigate existing multilingual and language-specific ASR systems.

The collected models will subsequently be evaluated using a common Kashmiri audio test dataset.

Fine-tuning will only be considered if the existing models fail to meet the project's accuracy or computational requirements.

## 2. Research Platforms

The following platforms will be used:

1. Hugging Face – pretrained models and checkpoints.
2. GitHub – model implementations and inference code.
3. AI4Bharat – Indian-language speech recognition research.
4. arXiv – research papers and technical documentation.
5. OpenSLR – speech datasets and language resources.

## 3. Initial Model Inventory

### Model 1: AI4Bharat IndicConformer (Kashmiri)

- Model: indicconformer_stt_ks_hybrid_ctc_rnnt_large
- Parameters: 120M encoder parameters, according to its model card.
- Architecture: Conformer-Large.
- Decoder: Hybrid CTC and RNN-T.
- Language: Kashmiri.
- Language code: ks.
- Input: 16 kHz mono-channel WAV.
- Output: Transcribed text.
- License: MIT.

Model: https://huggingface.co/ai4bharat/indicconformer_stt_ks_hybrid_ctc_rnnt_large

### Model 2: AI4Bharat IndicConformer Multilingual

- Model: indic-conformer-600m-multilingual
- Parameters: 600M.
- Architecture: Multilingual Conformer.
- Decoder: Hybrid CTC and RNN-T.
- Languages: 22 Indian languages, including Kashmiri.
- Language code: ks.
- License: MIT.

Model: https://huggingface.co/ai4bharat/indic-conformer-600m-multilingual

### Model 3: Indic-Transcribe Core

- Parameters: Approximately 1.2B.
- Base architecture: NVIDIA Canary.
- Encoder: FastConformer.
- Decoder: Transformer.
- Languages: 25 Indian languages, including Kashmiri.
- Features: Native-script transcription and automatic language identification.
- License: Indic Open License (verify terms before use).

Model: https://huggingface.co/bodhan-ai/indic-transcribe-core

### Model 4: Indic-Transcribe Flex

- Parameters: Approximately 1.2B.
- Base architecture: NVIDIA Canary.
- Languages: 27.
- Features: Flexible output modes, including native and alternative script representations.
- Kashmiri support: Yes.
- License: Verify model-specific terms before use.

Model: https://huggingface.co/bodhan-ai/indic-transcribe-flex

### Model 5: IndicASR

- Developed by AI4Bharat.
- Trained using the IndicVoices dataset.
- Supports 22 Indian languages, including Kashmiri.
- Includes multilingual speech recognition.
- Checkpoint and inference implementation are publicly referenced in the IndicVoices repository.

Repository: https://github.com/AI4Bharat/IndicVoices

Research paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.01926

Note: Verify whether the IndicASR checkpoint is distinct from the collected IndicConformer multilingual checkpoint before counting it as an independent model.

### Model 6: OpenAI Whisper

- Architecture: Transformer-based encoder-decoder.
- Available sizes: Tiny, Base, Small, Medium, Large and Turbo.
- Multilingual speech recognition.
- Kashmiri is not officially listed as a supported language.
- Will be considered an exploratory baseline rather than a primary candidate.

Repository: https://github.com/openai/whisper

### Model 7: Meta MMS

- Developed by Meta.
- Architecture: Multilingual wav2vec 2.0-based speech models.
- Available pretrained and fine-tuning checkpoints.
- Kashmiri availability must be verified before testing.
- License: CC-BY-NC 4.0 for the released MMS models.

Repository: https://github.com/facebookresearch/fairseq/tree/main/examples/mms

## 4. Dataset Research

The following dataset will be investigated:

**IndicVoices**

- Covers 22 Indian languages.
- Contains natural and spontaneous speech.
- Includes read, extempore and conversational recordings.
- Includes Kashmiri recordings.
- Provides a multilingual ASR training and inference pipeline.

Dataset: https://ai4bharat.iitm.ac.in/datasets/indicvoices

The exact number of Kashmiri recordings, hours of speech, transcript quality and regional dialect coverage must be verified.

## 5. Model Collection Strategy

At this stage, the team will:

1. Locate official model repositories.
2. Record model architecture and parameter count.
3. Identify supported languages and scripts.
4. Record model checkpoint sizes.
5. Check installation and inference requirements.
6. Record licenses and usage restrictions.
7. Collect available research papers.
8. Identify corresponding datasets and training methodologies.

No model will be fine-tuned during this task.

## 6. Future Evaluation Criteria

The collected models will later be evaluated using:

- Word Error Rate (WER).
- Character Error Rate (CER).
- Inference time.
- Memory consumption.
- GPU and CPU compatibility.
- Output script correctness.
- Performance across regional Kashmiri varieties.
- Performance on previously unseen speakers.

All models must be evaluated on the same independent test recordings and consistent text normalization rules.

